---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import Callout from '../../../components/docs/Callout.astro'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Playground"
  description="Try @attestto/verify live in the browser. Drop a PDF to verify or sign it — nothing leaves your device."
  currentPath="/docs/verify/playground/"
>
  <h1>Playground</h1>
  <p class="docs-hero-sub">
    Live demo of both components. Drop a PDF to verify or sign it.
    Everything runs in your browser &mdash; no data is transmitted.
  </p>

  <Callout type="privacy">
    <strong>Your documents never leave this device.</strong> The components below run entirely
    client-side. No files are uploaded, no hashes are sent, no analytics are collected.
  </Callout>

  <div class="playground-tabs" id="playground-tabs">
    <button class="playground-tab active" data-tab="verify">Verify</button>
    <button class="playground-tab" data-tab="sign">Sign</button>
  </div>

  <div class="playground-panel active" id="panel-verify">
    <attestto-verify theme="dark"></attestto-verify>
  </div>

  <div class="playground-panel" id="panel-sign">
    <attestto-sign theme="dark"></attestto-sign>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    // Load the verify web components
    var s = document.createElement('script')
    s.type = 'module'
    s.src = 'https://unpkg.com/@attestto/verify'
    document.head.appendChild(s)

    // Tab switching
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
      var tabs = document.querySelectorAll('.playground-tab')
      var panels = document.querySelectorAll('.playground-panel')

      tabs.forEach(function (tab) {
        tab.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var target = tab.getAttribute('data-tab')

          tabs.forEach(function (t) { t.classList.remove('active') })
          panels.forEach(function (p) { p.classList.remove('active') })

          tab.classList.add('active')
          document.getElementById('panel-' + target).classList.add('active')
        })
      })
    })
  </script>

  <style>
    .playground-tabs {
      display: flex;
      gap: 0;
      margin: 2rem 0 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--docs-border, #2a2a3a);
    }

    .playground-tab {
      padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
      background: none;
      border: none;
      border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
      color: var(--docs-text-muted, #8b8ba3);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: color 0.2s, border-color 0.2s;
    }

    .playground-tab:hover {
      color: var(--docs-text, #e2e2f0);
    }

    .playground-tab.active {
      color: var(--docs-brand, #594FD3);
      border-bottom-color: var(--docs-brand, #594FD3);
    }

    .playground-panel {
      display: none;
      padding: 2rem 0;
    }

    .playground-panel.active {
      display: block;
    }
  </style>

  <h2>What to try</h2>
  <div class="docs-steps">
    <div class="docs-step">
      <div class="docs-step-num">1</div>
      <div class="docs-step-body">
        <p><strong>Verify tab:</strong> Drop any PDF. The component will hash it, detect signatures, and run a forensic audit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-step">
      <div class="docs-step-num">2</div>
      <div class="docs-step-body">
        <p><strong>Signed PDFs:</strong> Try a digitally signed PDF (e.g., from Adobe Sign or Costa Rica Firma Digital) to see signature details and trust levels.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-step">
      <div class="docs-step-num">3</div>
      <div class="docs-step-body">
        <p><strong>Sign tab:</strong> Connect a DID wallet and sign a document. The result is a Verifiable Credential stored in your wallet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Embed this on your own site</h2>
  <p>This entire playground is just two HTML elements and one script tag:</p>

  <div class="docs-code-block">
    <div class="docs-code-header">
      <span>HTML</span>
      <button class="docs-code-copy" onclick="this.closest('.docs-code-block').querySelector('pre')?.textContent && navigator.clipboard.writeText(this.closest('.docs-code-block').querySelector('pre').textContent).then(() => { this.textContent = 'Copied!'; setTimeout(() => this.textContent = 'Copy', 1500) })">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <pre><Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-tag">&lt;script</span> <span class="c-attr">type</span>=<span class="c-str">"module"</span> <span class="c-attr">src</span>=<span class="c-str">"https://unpkg.com/@attestto/verify"</span><span class="c-tag">&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</span>
<span class="c-tag">&lt;attestto-verify&gt;&lt;/attestto-verify&gt;</span>
<span class="c-tag">&lt;attestto-sign&gt;&lt;/attestto-sign&gt;</span>`} /></pre>
  </div>

  <h2>See also</h2>
  <ul style="color: var(--docs-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 2; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
    <li><a href="/docs/verify/">Verify &amp; Sign overview</a> &mdash; architecture and trust levels</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/verify/installation/">Installation</a> &mdash; CDN, npm, and framework setup</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/verify/verify-component/">&lt;attestto-verify&gt; API</a> &mdash; full attribute and event reference</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/verify/sign-component/">&lt;attestto-sign&gt; API</a> &mdash; wallet-based signing</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/verify/theming/">Theming</a> &mdash; customize the look of both components</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
